{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I set them as heads</b> — אותם is plene with vav, to teach you that they had six traits, which we enumerated in the chapter of those strangled: Who is a son of the World to Come? — anyone who is humble of spirit, humble of deeds, enters and exits gently, grinds in Torah constantly, and does not attribute merit to himself. Officers of thousands and officers of hundreds and officers of fifties and officers of tens. Four forms of 'officers of' corresponding to the four banners. \"And officers for your tribes, and I will charge\" — an allusion to rod and strap; that He charged them to endure from the officers who would subdue them with rod and strap."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הנחנקין' refers to the four deaths by strangling in rabbinic law; 'six traits' likely means the six characteristics listed (humble of spirit, humble of deeds, enters gently, exits gently, grinds in Torah constantly, does not attribute merit to self). 'Four forms of שרי' refers to the four recurring instances of the word 'officers' in the list."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:31.196522188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}